{title: God the Father Be Our Stay}
{artist: Martin Luther · tr. Richard Massie}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 100}

Verse 1
[D]God [D]the Father, [D]be our Stay, [Bm]When [A]hell's [G]dread [Bm]pow'rs [A]assail
[D]us; Cleanse [D]us
from [D]our sins, we pray, [D]Nor [Bm]in our [A]last [D]hour fail
[D]us. [Bm]Keep [A]us from [A]the [D]Evil [Bm]One;
[F#m]Firm in [E]the [Em]faith
[D]abiding, [A]In [Em]Christ [Bm]our [C#m]Savior [D]hiding, [Em]And [D]heartily [D]confiding.
[G]Let [A]us put God's [D]armor [Bm]on:
[F#m]With [D]all [E]true Christians [D]running
[F#m]Our heav'nly [D]race [D]and shunning The [D]devil's [Bm]wiles [A]and [Em]cunning.
[D]Amen, [D]Amen, [D]this be done, So sing we, Hallelujah!

Verse 2
Jesus Christ be Thou our Stay, When hell's dread pow'rs assail
us; Cleanse us
from our sins, we pray, Nor in our last hour fail
us. Keep us from the Evil One;
Firm in the faith
abiding, In Christ our Savior hiding, And heartily confiding.
Let us put God's armor on:
With all true Christians running
Our heav'nly race and shunning The devil's wiles and cunning.
Amen, Amen, this be done, So sing we, Hallelujah!

Verse 3
Holy Ghost, be Thou our Stay, When hell's dread pow'rs assail
us; Cleanse us
from our sins, we pray, Nor in our last hour fail
us. Keep us from the Evil One;
Firm in the faith
abiding, In Christ our Savior hiding, And heartily confiding.
Let us put God's armor on:
With all true Christians running
Our heav'nly race and shunning The devil's wiles and cunning.
Amen, Amen, this be done, So sing we, Hallelujah!

Verse 4
1(alt). Triune God, be Thou our Stay, When hell's dread pow'rs assail
us; Cleanse us
from our sins, we pray, Nor in our last hour fail
us. Keep us from the Evil One;
Firm in the faith
abiding, In Christ our Savior hiding, And heartily confiding.
